# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Alexandre Peuch et al. (2026). Assessing the Transferability of General-Purpose MachineLearning Interatomic Potentials for Heterogeneous Catalysis with HetCat26.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2609.30621  arXiv:2609.30621v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2609.30621v1 (sha256 06487a2f54640c34...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 691 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/peuch2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the 15 foundation MLIPs evaluated as distributed on the
# HetCat26 benchmark (surface energies, adatom-vacancy formation,
# metal-oxide interactions, adsorption energies and site preferences,
# reaction barriers), with PBE (or PBE+D3) references, two data sets of
# which are new. All metrics are property errors (relative MAEs in %, with
# per-model MAEs in SI parity plots), so there are no results.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-peuch2026 a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Peuch et al. (2026): HetCat26, transferability of general-purpose MLIPs for heterogeneous catalysis" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-peuch2026 .

entity:article-peuch2026 a schema:ScholarlyArticle ;
    schema:sameAs <https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2609.30621> ;
    schema:datePublished "2026"^^xsd:gYear ;
    schema:name "Assessing the Transferability of General-Purpose MachineLearning Interatomic Potentials for Heterogeneous Catalysis with HetCat26" ;
    schema:author entity:person-Peuch-peuch2026 ,
        entity:person-KlerYoung-peuch2026 ,
        entity:person-Niu-peuch2026 ,
        entity:person-Hwang-peuch2026 ,
        entity:person-Mavrikakis-peuch2026 ,
        entity:person-Michaelides-peuch2026 ,
        entity:person-Berger-peuch2026 .

