###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - All benchmark metrics are property errors (relative errors in %, e.g. eSEN-30M-OAM 7.3% and MACE-MH-1-OMAT 11.3% average) or MAEs of surface, adsorption and barrier energies shown only in SI parity plots; inference costs are totals on one CPU shown in Fig. 2.
# - MatterSim-v1-5M is linked to the registry model MatterSim-v1. SevenNet is mapped to NequIP. HetCat26 (with new CADS34 and Cu barrier data) is a candidate data-set registry entry.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/peuch2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
